module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.QcohGlueAssembly
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fppf.CoveringSieves
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fppf.Precoverage

/-!
# Refining a covering family of the big fppf site to an fpqc covering family of the base

The descent datum of Stacks 03DX (1) is read off a covering family of the *final object* of
`(Sch/S)_fppf`, but it has to live on an fpqc covering family of the scheme `S` *downstairs*.
These are not the same thing: an object of the big fppf category over `S` is an arbitrary
scheme over `S`, so the structure morphisms of such a family need not even be flat, and only a
refinement of the sieve it generates is an fppf — hence fpqc — covering family of `S`.

This file supplies that refinement, and uses it to shrink the residue of Stacks 03DX (1)'s
gluing step.  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_coversTop_fpqc_refinement` turns a family
covering the final object into another such family whose *structure morphisms* are an fpqc
covering family of `S` and each of whose members maps into a member of the original family; the
residue `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.AssociatedModuleDatumOfRefinement` is then
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.AssociatedModuleGlueDescentDatum` with such a refinement handed
to it for free, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.associatedModuleDatumOfRefinement_iff` shows that nothing was
smuggled in while doing so.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.objHypercover`: a family of objects of `(Sch/S)_fppf`, read
  downstairs as the family of their structure morphisms `X i ⟶ S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.HasLocalAssociatedModule`: the restriction of a module on
  `(Sch/S)_fppf` to the big fppf site of the scheme of an object `T` is the associated module of
  a quasi-coherent sheaf there — the local datum that Stacks 03DX (1) obtains from Stacks 03DV
  and feeds to its gluing step.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.AssociatedModuleDatumOfRefinement`: **the descent datum of
  Stacks 03DX (1) as a hypothesis, with the passage to an fpqc covering family of `S` already
  performed** — the residue of the gluing step after this file.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_coversTop_fppf_refinement` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_coversTop_fpqc_refinement`: **every family covering the
  final object of `(Sch/S)_fppf` is refined by one whose structure morphisms are an fppf — hence
  an fpqc — covering family of `S`.**  The members of the refinement are the sources of the
  flat, locally finitely presented, jointly surjective family that the covering sieve of the
  final object generated by the given family contains.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.associatedModuleGlueDescentDatum_of_datumOfRefinement`: the
  residue implies `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.AssociatedModuleGlueDescentDatum`, the
  refinement being supplied by the previous result and the local isomorphisms of the conclusion
  being the restrictions of a global one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.datumOfRefinement_of_associatedModuleGlueDescentDatum` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.associatedModuleDatumOfRefinement_iff`: the converse, hence the
  equivalence — the residue is **not** a strengthening of the hypothesis it replaces.

## Implementation notes

Nothing here carries a `stacks` attribute: every statement about a clause of Stacks 03DX is
still conditional, and a hypothesis is part of a citation.

The index universe is `u + 1` throughout, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.EssImageAssociatedModuleQcohGlue`: the covering families of the
final object of `(Sch/S)_fppf` that Stacks 03DN produces are indexed by the objects of that
site, which form a `Type (u + 1)`, and the family produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_family_of_mem_topology` is indexed at the same universe.

The refinement is extracted from the covering sieve `Sieve.ofObjects X` of the final object
rather than from the family `X` itself: that sieve is covering precisely because `X` covers the
final object, and `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_family_of_mem_topology` — the big-site half of
Stacks 021R and 021S — returns a family inside it whose morphisms of schemes are flat, locally
of finite presentation and jointly surjective.  Those three properties are exactly membership in
the fppf precoverage of all schemes, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme`
`.fppfPrecoverage_le_fpqcPrecoverage` finishes.  The members of the family are produced as
objects over the final object `Over.mk (𝟙 S)`, so their structure morphisms over `S` carry a
spurious composition with an identity; they are therefore reindexed through the canonical
isomorphism `Over.mk (m j) ≅ Over.mk (m j ≫ 𝟙 S)`, which is also what carries the
factorisations through `X` to the refinement.

What remains in the residue is the big-site ⟷ descent-data bridge: the associated-module
comparison `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.associatedModuleObjIso` of Stacks 03DV exists at each
object of the big site and is natural in the module, but its *functoriality in the object* — the
square relating it at `T` and at `T'` for a morphism `T' ⟶ T` — is not in the library, and that
square is what turns the local isomorphisms into the transition data of a descent datum.  The
transition isomorphisms themselves and their cocycle condition would then come from full
faithfulness of `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` over the binary and triple fibre products
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.full_associatedModuleQcoh_of_fpqcDescent` and
`…faithful_associatedModuleQcoh_of_fpqcDescent`, both unconditional once fed
`AlgebraicGeometry.fpqcDescentOfQuasicoherentHoms`), and the datum could be presented on the
chosen fibre products through `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData'.descentData` rather
than at every object of the site at once.

